 "parts": [
  "In one big study, about one in four people said they sneeze at the sun.",
  "That study surveyed more than three thousand people in China.",
  "So why does bright light make your nose tickle?",
  "Scientists still don't fully know.",
  "You might think that's rare. It's not.",
  "Is it just one gene? Also no.",
  "In twenty ten, researchers surveyed customers of a genetics company.",
  "They found a spot on chromosome two linked to it.",
  "In twenty nineteen, the study in China found that same spot.",
  "The authors' conclusion: it's complex, not a simple one-gene trait.",
  "So what happens in the brain? A small study recorded the brain activity of ten sneezers and ten other people.",
  "The sneezers' vision center reacted more strongly, even to a plain checkerboard.",
  "The authors say it's more than a classic brainstem reflex.",
  "But they can't rule out the brainstem playing a role.",
  "So look around the dinner table.",
  "Maybe one of every four people there sneezes at the sun, and science still can't fully explain it."
 ],
